# Vantress Visions targets "activated or triggered ability you control" (CR 115.1, 113.3): not a spell on the stack, and not an
# ability Bot2 controls. Bot2's Walking Ballista (X = 1) is refused while it is a spell, and its "remove a counter: 1 damage"
# ability, once on the stack, is refused too; Visions is never cast, so nothing is exiled on an adventure and Bot1 takes 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Virtue of Knowledge
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Walking Ballista
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Virtue of Knowledge.Cast(Stack.Walking Ballista; Ability: Vantress Visions)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Activate(Bot1; Ability: Remove)
! Bot1.Hand.Virtue of Knowledge.Cast(Stack.Walking Ballista; Ability: Vantress Visions)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

